                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_484">Salisbury, Wiltshire. Cathedral
                        church of St Mary the Virgin; see removed from Sherborne in 1078</orgName><p>A detached fragment of Salisbury Cathedral 167, being quires
                        a--c and the first two leaves of quire d. Seen by John Leland at Salisbury:
                        he quotes the title. Table of contents of the first four items on fol. 57,
                        with item 3 and 4 still in Salisbury 167.</p><p>In Salisbury 167, a note (s.
                        xvii) reads 'Philobiblon exsecta'; it had been cut out before Young
                        catalogue the manuscripts in 1621.</p></provenance>
